<title>MOLDOVA: Moldova 28-, 91-day T-bills down, 182-, 364-day up.</title>
<headline>Moldova 28-, 91-day T-bills down, 182-, 364-day up.</headline>
<dateline>CHISINAU 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised yield on Moldovan 28-day Treasury bills fell to 17.17 percent on Tuesday from 18.51 percent at the previous auction on July 29, the National Bank said.</p>
<p>The yield on 91-day T-bills went down to 16.71 percent from 20.22 percent on July 29.</p>
<p>The yield on 182-day T-bills rose to 18.87 percent from 18.63 percent on July 29.</p>
<p>The yield on 364-day T-bills were 20.83 percent after 20.10 percent on July 29.</p>
<p>Full details of the 28-day T-bill auction:</p>
<p>				    Aug 5		July 29</p>
<p> Issue volume		   2.00 million lei     2.00 million lei</p>
<p> Denominations		  1,000 lei	  1,000 lei</p>
<p> Nominal demand		 2.85 million	   3.35 million</p>
<p> Volume sold		    2.00 million	   2.00 million</p>
<p> Yield			    17.17 pct	  18.51 pct</p>
<p> Price			    98.70 pct	  98.60 pct</p>
<p> Range of bids		  98.70-99.00 pct  98.60-99.00 pct</p>
<p> Maturity			 Sep 4, 1997	Aug 28, 1997</p>
